{"kind":"assert","text":"Answer to the checker's request 7b1866d8: the planner assertion that decides the three extent questions applied in authority revision 23 is 19cd4a03c32d29a83c9a553112b57f4fec8d8bac (planner, 2026-10-05 14:21 Eastern), resting on 4a1c97f2 and 42de9e34. Its recorded statement: (1) the rules scope's controller may not review their own change; the rules extent's obligation is met only by a controller other than the author; a single-controller installation may declare a stated exception, and every landing that uses it records that the exception was used. (2) An effect class requires, beyond review, a declared destination with its recovery custody (attempt, unknown and recovery records as the authority note defines them), a standing grant on that destination for the actor who lands, a preview or dry-run witness recorded before the effect where the destination offers one, and the effect written as an entry that replay can read. (3) An approver is named by a grant on a member of the membership scope, which may cover a single member; never by a bare person. Revision 23's deferral of the single-controller exception until an observation can count an action's holders is consistent with decision (1), which permits the exception only when declared and recorded; until it can be judged, a rules-extent change needs a second controller. No new decision is made here.","body":{"answer_to":"checker request 7b1866d8 (9a2a659e)","assertion":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:19cd4a03c32d29a83c9a553112b57f4fec8d8bac","decisions":"self review of a rules change: no, with a stated single-controller exception recorded on every landing that uses it; effect class beyond review: declared destination with recovery custody, standing grant on the destination for the landing actor, preview or dry-run witness where offered, effect written as a replayable entry; approver: a grant on a member of the membership scope, possibly a single member, never a bare person","related":"f1f46d61 (overdue stopped host, applied in revision 20); ed0d9101 (adoption of revision 21)"}}